DTSTAMP:20260924T115707Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250317
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250318
SUMMARY:Wisconsin: Form 3 (partnership) / Form 5S (S-corp) due
DESCRIPTION:Wisconsin partnership return due the 15th day of the 3rd month 
 after year-end. Correction (this rebuild session): the cited source states 
 the general rule (15th day of the 3rd month) without addressing the 2026-sp
 ecific weekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sunday. Consistent with e
 very other state in this data set that explicitly confirms a weekend-shift 
 policy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Delaware\, Montana\, Oreg
 on all confirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and with the near-universal U
 S government-deadline convention of shifting to the next business day\, thi
 s entry's date_2026 was corrected from an unshifted March 15\, 2026 to Marc
 h 16\, 2026. This is a computed application of the general shift convention
 \, not an independently re-fetched per-state confirmation that this specifi
 c state's statute shifts - flagged here for transparency. | Wisconsin partn
 ership return due the 15th day of the 3rd month after year-end. Automatic w
 ith the federal extension - attach a copy to the Wisconsin return\; no sepa
 rate WI extension form needed for filing (payment still due by the original
  date). Correction (this rebuild session): the cited source states the gene
 ral rule (15th day of the 3rd month) without addressing the 2026-specific w
 eekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sunday. Consistent with every oth
 er state in this data set that explicitly confirms a weekend-shift policy (
 e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Delaware\, Montana\, Oregon all c
 onfirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and with the near-universal US govern
 ment-deadline convention of shifting to the next business day\, this entry'
 s date_2026 was corrected from an unshifted March 15\, 2026 to March 16\, 2
 026. This is a computed application of the general shift convention\, not a
 n independently re-fetched per-state confirmation that this specific state'
 s statute shifts - flagged here for transparency. | Authority: Wisconsin De
 partment of Revenue\, direct fetch of the current Form 3 instructions PDF t
 his session: "A partnership must file its return with the department by the
  15th day of the 3rd month following the close of its taxable year" and "An
 y extension allowed by the Internal Revenue Service (IRS)... automatically 
 extends the Wisconsin due date\, if you include a copy of the federal exten
 sion." (An earlier same-session automated fetch of a DOR FAQ page had misst
 ated this as "June 15" - that figure was rejected and replaced with this di
 rectly-quoted instructions PDF text\, which controls.) | Source: https://ww
 w.revenue.wi.gov/TaxForms2025/2025-Form3-Inst.pdf | This date is computed f
 rom a recurrence rule and may not reflect a later-announced change\; confir
 m against the cited source before relying on it.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
